    "explanation": "To both parties. Trip TRP-02818 ran 14.44 km on the platform's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-02818, gps_trace.trace_distance_km) against a booked optimal of 12.00 km (EV-TRIP-02818) — an excess of 2.44 km, or 20.33%. Both POL-RD-01 gates are passed (greater than 0.80 km and greater than 20% of optimal), so a route deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not MATERIAL (20.33% is below 50% and 2.44 km is below 8.0 km), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged and the driver_profile check adds nothing: no repeat-deviation pattern is established in any event (deviation_flags_90d = 1 against completed_trips_90d = 188, below both the 3-flag and 0.05-ratio tests), so there is no POL-RD-06(b) full-refund uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07: 114 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum inter-fix gap of 0 s, so no independent corroboration was required and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises.\n\nThe driver's explanation ('a minor detour because of a road works sign') cannot be run and does not exonerate. The bundle holds no traffic advisory for this trip: EV-ADVIS-02818-01 is MISSING, its issue code is MISSING_ARTIFACT and its weight_multiplier is 0.0. POL-RD-03 is therefore unavailable, and under POL-RD-08 the assertion carries no weight. Because the driver named no advisory identifier, POL-RD-13(1) makes this a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) does not fire and the case is decided on the recorded trace rather than escalated. The assertion is discarded and no advisory was on file. No pickup or dropoff relocation occurred (POL-RD-05: no amendment timestamps, no stored re-quote), and the chat log for this trip carries 0 messages, so there is no rider instruction and no waypoint_hint against which POL-RD-04 could run. Nothing reduces the measured excess.\n\nUnder POL-RD-02 (fare_model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not apply; the surge multiplier of 1.0